        {
          "url": "https://soli.openlegalstandard.org/RCcWasK7LnVMXipm7uQAOA2",
          "text": "A visitor is an individual who temporarily enters a specific location, such as a country, city, or residence, for various purposes. Visitors can include tourists, who travel for leisure and exploration; business visitors, who come for work-related activities; or guests invited to a residence for social or personal reasons. The nature of the visit and applicable regulations, such as visa requirements or entry permissions, can differ based on the visitor's purpose and destination.",
